# ── THE REGISTER AND ITS VIEWS: union merge ──────────────────────────────────
# These are APPEND-ONLY tables that every node writes to.  A union merge keeps
# both sides' added lines, which is exactly right here and exactly wrong
# everywhere else -- so it is declared on these paths and no others.
#
# ** Union merge cannot detect a duplicate ID. **  That is why the ID bands in
# THE_HUB.md exist and why corpus/check_id_bands.py runs in CI.
THE_LIVE_ARC.md      merge=union
WHATS_TEED_UP.md     merge=union
THE_BURN_DOWN.md     merge=union
CORPUS_MAP.md        merge=union

# ── NO LFS.  CORRECTED r2419, and the earlier advice was wrong. ──────────────
# r2407 put pdf/png/eps/dat behind git-lfs.  ** Measured before pushing: the
# largest file in the tree is 4.3 MB (CORPUS_MAP.md) and the whole tree is
# 72 MB. **  GitHub's hard limit is 100 MB per FILE and it warns at 50 MB; the
# repo soft limit is 1 GB.  ** Nothing here is within an order of magnitude of
# any limit. **
#
# So LFS would buy nothing and cost a dependency: a clone made without git-lfs
# installed silently yields POINTER FILES instead of content, which is exactly
# the kind of failure that looks like data loss.  ** An instrument that adds a
# failure mode without removing one is not worth installing. **
#
# If a future addition ever approaches 50 MB, revisit -- and note it here.

# ── text, so diffs read ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md   text
*.tex  text
*.py   text
*.sh   text
